[00:01:13.897] The screen registered a hardware input when the side/power button was pressed on the right side of the device, prompting the power HUD—rendered as a black, vertically oriented, thin elongated capsule—to appear dynamically along the right margin of the display. 
[00:01:14.358] A modal prompt titled "Turn On Siri" animates into view, sliding upward from the bottom of the display. The prompt is visually organized with the following elements:
•	Header/Title: "Siri" rendered in large bold typography.
•	Body Text: Descriptive text reading: "Siri helps you find information and get things done, just by asking. To use Siri, press and hold the side button. Speak when Siri appears."
•	Legal disclaimer: Apple stores transcripts of your interactions with Siri and may review a subset of these transcripts. Siri may also send information like your voice input. Siri setup, contacts, and location to Apple to process your request. Data is not associated with your Apple Account. About Siri…
•	Interactive Action Buttons: Two horizontal system buttons:
o	"Turn On Siri" (blue background with white letters)
o	" Don’t Use Siri" (borderless button, with blue letters)
[00:01:15.446] The screen registered a hardware input when the volume down button was pressed on the left side of the device, prompting the system volume HUD—rendered as a black, vertically oriented, thin elongated capsule—to appear dynamically along the left margin of the display.
At this point, two vertical capsules are visible simultaneously on opposing edges of the display. 
[00:01:16.404] The Turn On Siri screen suddenly disappears, and the Journal App's Settings interface is on view
[00:01:16.535] And odd status bar behavior begins as it begins to fade and slide right in to view. This status bar associated with the hard reset interface.
[00:01:16.832] The status bar slides so far to the right, that the Connectivity & Power related icons go out of view, and the system time and silence icon are partially visible to the right of the dynamic island--which was transformed from an elongated black shape pill with a solid red circular indicator on its left side to a narrower black shaped pill without any indicators.
[00:01:17.789] Suddenly, the elements of the status bar shift to their usual place, with the system time and silence icon on the left of the dynamic island and the Connectivity & Power icons on the right side. 
[00:01:17.888] The dynamic island begins to fade out of view
[00:01:17.987] The dynamic island reappears fully in to view
[00:01:18.119] The dynamic island suddenly completely disappears.
[00:01:18.350] Finally, the power-off and emergency response interface overlays the display. 
•	The interface is visually organized into two principal areas: the status area, and the content area:
o	Status Bar: Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
	Time: Displays the local time as 09:26. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
	Connectivity & Power: The cellular signal strength icon displays three solid black bars and one gray bar, followed by the network type indicator ("5GUW"). The adjacent battery icon appears partially filled alongside the digital readout "61."
o	Interface Body composed of the following three buttons: 
	Slide to power off: A horizontal interactive slider control positioned near the top of the interface, accompanied by the text label "slide to power off" and an accompanying circular power icon.
	Emergency Call: A horizontal interactive slider control positioned in the middle of the interface, accompanied by the text label "Emergency Call" and an accompanying circular SOS icon, with the explanatory text "Slide to call emergency Services" below
	Cancel: A command button located at the bottom of the display labeled "Cancel" to dismiss the interface.
